## MIGRATION REFERENCE

### Category A: Puppet Built-in Replacements

These deprecated functions have direct Puppet built-in equivalents on Puppet 6+.

| Deprecated | Replacement | Example |
|-----------|-------------|---------|
| `abs($val)` | `$val.abs` | Built-in since Puppet 6.0 |
| `camelcase($str)` | `$str.camelcase` | Built-in since Puppet 6.0 |
| `capitalize($str)` | `$str.capitalize` | Built-in since Puppet 6.0 |
| `ceiling($num)` | `$num.ceiling` | Built-in since Puppet 6.0 |
| `chomp($str)` | `$str.chomp` | Built-in since Puppet 6.0 |
| `chop($str)` | `$str.chop` | Built-in since Puppet 6.0 |
| `dig($data, ['a','b'])` | `$data.dig('a', 'b')` | Individual keys, not array |
| `dig44($data, ['a','b'])` | `$data.dig('a', 'b')` | Spread array keys |
| `downcase($str)` | `$str.downcase` | Built-in since Puppet 6.0 |
| `empty($var)` | `$var.empty` | Built-in since Puppet 5.5 |
| `flatten($arr)` | `$arr.flatten` | Built-in since Puppet 5.5 |
| `floor($num)` | `$num.floor` | Built-in since Puppet 6.0 |
| `getvar('mod::var')` | `$mod::var` | Direct variable access preferred |
| `has_key($hash, 'k')` | `'k' in $hash` | `in` operator — note arg reversal |
| `hash(['a',1,'b',2])` | `Hash(['a',1,'b',2])` | Type constructor |
| `join($arr, ', ')` | `$arr.join(', ')` | Built-in since Puppet 6.0 |
| `keys($hash)` | `$hash.keys` | Built-in since Puppet 6.0 |
| `length($var)` | `$var.length` | Built-in since Puppet 5.5 |
| `lstrip($str)` | `$str.lstrip` | Built-in since Puppet 6.0 |
| `max($a, $b)` | `max($a, $b)` or `[$a,$b].max` | Built-in since Puppet 6.0 |
| `min($a, $b)` | `min($a, $b)` or `[$a,$b].min` | Built-in since Puppet 6.0 |
| `private()` | `assert_private()` | Rename — still requires stdlib |
| `round($num)` | `$num.round` | Built-in since Puppet 6.0 |
| `rstrip($str)` | `$str.rstrip` | Built-in since Puppet 6.0 |
| `size($var)` | `$var.length` | Use `length` instead |
| `sort($arr)` | `$arr.sort` | Built-in since Puppet 5.5 |
| `sprintf_hash(fmt, h)` | `sprintf(fmt, h)` | Built-in since Puppet 4.10 |
| `strip($str)` | `$str.strip` | Built-in since Puppet 6.0 |
| `try_get_value($d, 'a/b')` | `$d.dig('a', 'b')` | Use dig with individual keys |
| `type($var)` | `type($var)` | Built-in returns Type object, not string |
| `type3x($var)` | `type($var)` | Same as above |
| `unique($arr)` | `$arr.unique` | Built-in since Puppet 5.5 |
| `upcase($str)` | `$str.upcase` | Built-in since Puppet 6.0 |
| `values($hash)` | `$hash.values` | Built-in since Puppet 6.0 |

### Category B: Type-System Replacements (is_* functions)

Replace `is_*` type-checking functions with Puppet `=~ Type` match expressions.

| Deprecated | Replacement |
|-----------|-------------|
| `is_absolute_path($var)` | `$var =~ Stdlib::Absolutepath` (still needs stdlib) |
| `is_array($var)` | `$var =~ Array` |
| `is_bool($var)` | `$var =~ Boolean` |
| `is_domain_name($var)` | `$var =~ Stdlib::Fqdn` (still needs stdlib) |
| `is_email_address($var)` | `$var =~ Stdlib::Email` (still needs stdlib) |
| `is_float($var)` | `$var =~ Float` |
| `is_function_available($f)` | No replacement — remove or use `defined()` |
| `is_hash($var)` | `$var =~ Hash` |
| `is_integer($var)` | `$var =~ Integer` |
| `is_ip_address($var)` | `$var =~ Stdlib::IP::Address` (still needs stdlib) |
| `is_ipv4_address($var)` | `$var =~ Stdlib::IP::Address::V4` |
| `is_ipv6_address($var)` | `$var =~ Stdlib::IP::Address::V6` |
| `is_mac_address($var)` | `$var =~ Stdlib::MAC` (still needs stdlib) |
| `is_numeric($var)` | `$var =~ Numeric` |
| `is_string($var)` | `$var =~ String` |

### Category C: Validation Function Replacements (validate_* functions)

**Path 1 — Class parameters (preferred):**

```puppet
# Before:
class mymod ($path, $packages, $enabled) {
  validate_absolute_path($path)
  validate_array($packages)
  validate_bool($enabled)
}

# After:
class mymod (
  Stdlib::Absolutepath $path,
  Array $packages,
  Boolean $enabled,
) {
}
```

**Path 2 — Mid-manifest (use assert_type):**

```puppet
# Before:
validate_hash($data)

# After:
assert_type(Hash, $data)
```

**Type mappings:**

| Deprecated | Type Parameter |
|-----------|---------------|
| `validate_absolute_path` | `Stdlib::Absolutepath` |
| `validate_array` | `Array` |
| `validate_bool` | `Boolean` |
| `validate_hash` | `Hash` |
| `validate_integer` | `Integer` (with min/max: `Integer[$min, $max]`) |
| `validate_ip_address` | `Stdlib::IP::Address` |
| `validate_ipv4_address` | `Stdlib::IP::Address::V4` |
| `validate_ipv6_address` | `Stdlib::IP::Address::V6` |
| `validate_numeric` | `Numeric` |
| `validate_re($v, '^pat$')` | `Pattern[/^pat$/]` |
| `validate_slength($v, 10)` | `String[0, 10]` (or `String[min, max]`) |
| `validate_string` | `String` |
| `validate_legacy(Type, ..)` | Remove — use `Type` directly in parameter |

